A||N||2||Lewis||Cleaning throttle body||||5||
Z||000000||Lewis||05-31-2000||10:02 PM||||I removed the plastic tube to my throttle body and stuck my finger in it and found a lot of black soot and greasy grime.  I know it has to be cleaned.  Can I open up the flap that is inside and spray in it or do I have to keep it closed?  Also how do I remove the IAC to clean it?||||reg||5
Z||000001||GT Bastard||06-01-2000||01:31 AM||||Get some sort of spray cleaner... I used the Holly stuff.  Open the butterfly and hose it down.  Then just use a rag to wipe off the grime.  Too much grime can cause the butterfly to stick.  Just use a wrench on the IAC, and be careful.  You'll need a new gasket too.  I've heard of people useing q-tips to clearn the pintle on it.  Haven't tried it myself yet.||||reg||1
Z||000002||AL||06-01-2000||08:22 PM||||take the iac out and clean it with break cleaner spray, then spray the inside of the throttle even on the plate and everywhere else, then check the pintle on the iac and then put it back in and your done. the reason i say break cleaner is because it cleans and dries fast.||||reg||1
